From e61976170bc051b92500c672a633760298081887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan McCallum <apt-install-coffee@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:43:39 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 146/146] firmware: arm_scmi: restore ACPI boot support for CIX
 Sky1

The v7.2 SCMI transport rework (scmi_transport_supplier) led to the
fork's ACPI-boot SCMI support being dropped, on the assumption that the
Orion O6 boots via device tree. Hosts that boot with acpi=on lose SCMI
entirely: the ACPI clock provider (CIXHA010, clk-sky1-acpi) defers
waiting for SCMI clocks that never appear, and the VPU (CIXH3010) along
with ~120 other platform devices is held indefinitely by fw_devlink in
waiting_for_supplier - no /dev/video0, no hardware video decode.

Port the ACPI SCMI semantics onto the v7.2 transport design:

- bus.c: scmi_dev inherits its parent fwnode when it has no DT node
- common.h: DEFINE_SCMI_TRANSPORT_DRIVER grows an __acpi_match
  parameter again and propagates the transport device fwnode to the
  arm-scmi platform device when no DT node is present
- driver.c: ACPI base-protocol enumeration fallback (SCMI_NO_DT_NODE
  sentinel in active_protocols) plus shared base-channel fallback in
  scmi_chan_setup for non-base protocols
- shmem.c: ACPI shared-memory discovery via _DSD 'shmem' references
  (CIXHA004/CIXHA005), honouring reg-io-width for the I/O ops
- transports/mailbox.c: CIXHA006 ACPI match, ACPI _DSD mbox/shmem
  reference counting for channel validation, and early chan_available
  when of_node is NULL
- transports/optee,smc,virtio: pass NULL ACPI match

The mailbox core ACPI fwnode lookup and cix-mailbox overlapping-region
handling were untouched by the transport rework and remain in place.

The device-tree boot path is unchanged: every added code path is
guarded on a missing of_node.
